sha256  271d843e04be2d24af3c254b6c058e9478dfb4db01989656d68ce67abde11e26  bmcd-ed5d997ca7fb16b450fd8cfa2bf9811f49110a55-cargo2.tar.gz
#
# 2.42.0 (6011cfd8, tag v2.42.0): says when the board is not keeping its
# settings, and repairs it. GET /api/bmc/storage reports the state, reading
# /etc/safemode.reason (written by /sbin/preinit); KEY1 always wins, so a
# board held in safe mode by the button is reported as requested whatever the
# file says; the factory-password gate opens
# only the two storage endpoints (status and repair); POST
# /api/bmc/storage/repair erases the settings volume and reboots. Needs the
# firmware that writes /etc/safemode.reason (v2.46.0) for the detail.
#
# Measured 2026-10-31: the PR build in CI's own container (run 41223040725),
# against a placeholder line, reported got 090165eb; this is that value.
sha256  090165eba78dcf71305fdff9e08965ace8d71f901e907ed7537f926257393d1e  bmcd-6011cfd85e8eb65e91839df59069b9ff5e626469-cargo2.tar.gz
#
# 2.42.1 (cac4adb2, tag v2.42.1): the storage repair added in 2.42.0 is
# offered on a real board. The kernel mounts the read-only image itself, so
# /proc/mounts names the root /dev/root, which is not a device node, and 2.42.0
# reported backing "unknown" and never offered the repair. When the mount
# source of the read-only root is /dev/root (or not a device node), bmcd now
# resolves the kernel's root= from /proc/cmdline (MAJOR:MINOR through
# /sys/class/block/*/dev, or /dev/<name> as it stands). Anything unresolvable
# stays unknown and still blocks the repair. Nothing else changed.
#
# Measured 2026-10-31: the PR build in CI's own container (run 41227540168),
# against a placeholder line, reported got d5622c55; this is that value.
sha256  d5622c55fcb7b84a7c0cd693a3134a104cdfc9f69394a3616e864c4a87ffed18  bmcd-cac4adb2477348ee265dd250cf2b98a6ca4f1ae4-cargo2.tar.gz
#
# 2.42.2 (3c15da5d, tag v2.42.2): a board with no SD card (or a card without a
# firmware folder) no longer retries the whole firmware check every two
# minutes with a warning: the SD card source reports nothing when the card is
# not mounted. The "no card" refusal for parking says installing directly is
# the way out. A successful park marks the cached catalogue stale. Each
# firmware source has its own 360 s deadline (the updater runs in its own
# process group and is killed as a group), so one hung source no longer
# discards the others' answers. GET /api/bmc/info gains `mounted` on the
# "SD card" storage entry. Nothing else changed.
#
# Measured 2026-11-01: the PR build in CI's own container (run 41316762877),
